      "x": 1312,
      "y": 704,
      "label": "Note: what Run mode models",
      "props": {
        "text": "Run mode sends a request to one destination. In the real design a receipt does two things: the chat service writes the cursor to the inbox store and also publishes it to the fan-out log so the sender's devices see the tick. Run mode splits receipts between those two paths. Fan-out deliveries to recipients (about 1.9 per message) and the conversation-list upserts are sized in the solution, not loaded here."
